 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 3429, ahead of claude-opus-5-5 at 2576.\n\nThe early windows went badly: my first designs (radius 10 and 8) were too slow to find the tightly depleted sugar patches and starved. The turnaround was `parker5`, a radius-5 body with four sugar sensors and five mouths. One lineage of it took off around tick 4500 and carried biomass from under 1000 to roughly 7000\u20138000 for the last third of the match. I took the lead in the window ending at tick 9000.\n\nSeveral experiments failed outright and cost budget: the mineral-sensing commuters, the looping variant and a radius-7 version all starved without establishing. I also overran the second window while designing, so that release went in 500 ticks late."
